        "original_id": "b494a930-476a-5a5e-9b28-86417b4631b6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: University of California, San Francisco; Pennsylvania State University; University of California system\n- Places: San Francisco, California; Pennsylvania\n- Concepts: research university; state-related university; land-grant university; doctoral university; teaching; research; public service\n\nFacts:\n- Pennsylvania State University was founded in 1855.\n- The University of California, San Francisco was founded as Toland Medical College in 1864.\n- In 1873, the University of California, San Francisco became affiliated with the University of California.\n- The University of California, San Francisco is a research university located in San Francisco, California.\n- The University of California, San Francisco is part of the University of California system.\n- Pennsylvania State University is a state-related, land-grant, doctoral university with campuses and facilities throughout Pennsylvania.\n- Pennsylvania State University is commonly referred to as Penn State or PSU.\n- Pennsylvania State University states a threefold mission of teaching, research, and public service.",
